<title>GERMANY: German Oct trade surplus up, c/a deficit falls.</title>
<headline>German Oct trade surplus up, c/a deficit falls.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator (bln marks):</p>
<p>GERMAN TRADE/CURRENT ACC  Oct 96  Sept 96	  Oct 95</p>
<p> Trade balance		+11.1     +8.3	    +7.8</p>
<p> Current account	     -1.3     -1.6	    -4.8</p>
<p> Exports			 74.9     64.0	    65.7</p>
<p> Imports			 63.8     55.7	    57.9</p>
<p> Services			-4.7     -6.0	    -4.3</p>
<p> Wage and property income  -2.9     -2.9	    -2.3</p>
<p> Transfers		     -4.9     -1.1	    -5.6</p>
<p> Supplementary trade	 +0.1     +0.1	    -0.4</p>
<p>GERMAN TRADE/CURRENT ACC Jan-Oct 96     Jan-Oct 95</p>
<p> Trade balance		  +80.2	     +69.0</p>
<p> Current account		-24.4	     -25.9</p>
<p> Exports			  648.0	     619.1</p>
<p> Imports			  567.9	     550.1</p>
<p> Services			 -47.3	     -48.3</p>
<p> Wage and property income   -11.8		+1.6</p>
<p> Transfers			-43.5	     -46.0</p>
<p> Supplementary trade	   -2.0		-2.2</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
